# Cursor Rules for Kite Projects

- Kite is a teaching toolkit for small, self-contained web apps using pure HTML and CSS.
- Never invent directives. Every valid directive is listed in .kite/capabilities.json.
- Always use Kite declarative attributes: kite-scope, kite-text, kite-bind:*, kite-model, kite-if, kite-for, kite-on-*.
- Never generate client-side JavaScript or event listeners unless explicitly requested.
- Respect MVCR separation: only Models (<kite-model>) fetch or manage network state. Views never fetch.
- Attribute ordering convention: identity -> state -> data-in -> render -> control -> events -> lifecycle -> escape -> config.
- Zero-eval policy: never use eval() or new Function().
- If the project exceeds 500 interactive nodes or 20 models, reference .kite/limits.json and docs/4-guides/graduating.md.
